%N A400197 The union of the squares (A000290) and the integer 2.
%C A400197 The significance of this sequence lies in the fact that it is simpler to prove that its Heraclitus transform (A400196) contains every integer than it is to prove the same for the Heraclitus transform of the squares (A377091).
%H A400197 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400197/b400197.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400197 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,-3,1).
%F A400197 From _Jianing Song_, Oct 01 2026: (Start)
%F A400197 G.f.: x*(1 + x)*(1 - 2*x + 3*x^2 - x^3)/(1 - x)^3.
%F A400197 E.g.f: -1 + x + x^2/2 + (1 - x + x^2)*exp(x). (End)
%t A400197 Union[{2}, Range[0, 50]^2] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 01 2026 *)
%Y A400197 Cf. A000290, A400196, A377091.
